;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "denotational_design_with_type_class_morphisms-long"
 :source "denotational_design_with_type_class_morphisms-long.pdf"
 :page 2
 :exercises "The split display number, and tight furniture the band cannot see.

The page sets \"2.\" and \"Denotational semantics and data types\" as
two records on one baseline, one face (NimbusRomNo9L-Medi, 1.23 body
heights), 0.018 apart - a gap between both join branches by design:
the number ends on its dot, the title opens uppercase, no dot chain.
The same-face bare-number branch rejoins them, and the outline's
title then places at the joined line behind its section number.
Before the join, the number rendered as a stray line above the
placed heading.

The running head and its corner folio sit at baseline 0.065 with the
body starting right under them, and the head runs as wide as a
column - never narrow, never folio-merged.  The profile's text span
is what drops them: the folio is a bare page marker above the modal
body start, and the head shares its baseline.  The head alternates
corners with the folio page by page and on odd pages starts exactly
at the text edge at full column measure, which is why a line on a
marker's baseline can never anchor the span."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0 :glued 0))
